# Application structural roles (documentation only).
#
# The graph entity is identity (ID-ONE). No coordinate schema here.
# APPLICATION-FACT-CLOSURE — one authoritative owner per dimension:
#
# relation     unique `.binding` edge from occurrence
# subject      unique `.projection` at application_subject_projection
# operands     packed application_values range (ApplicationFact.arguments)
# results      packed application_values range (ApplicationFact.results)
# descriptor   application node.descriptor (occurrence)
# demand       application node.demand (occurrence)
# effect       ApplicationFact.effect Card
# authority    ApplicationFact.authority Card
# witness      ApplicationFact.witness Card
# stage        application node.stage (occurrence)
# caller       application node.scope (home of occurrence)
# target       ApplicationFact.target Card
# realization  ApplicationFact.realization Card
# provenance   application node.span / provenanceOf
#
# FACT-CARDINALITY-ONE: Card = unknown | none | one(id). Never ?id = null.
#
# Query accessors (`law.application.consumer`, `law.fact.locality`):
# applicationRelation applicationCaller applicationSubject
# applicationArguments applicationResults applicationDescriptor
# applicationDemand applicationStage applicationProvenance
# applicationsIn(home) borrowed occurrence range — never scan all applications
# relationsReferencedBy(home) unique relation ids from that range
# effect/authority/witness/target/realization via ApplicationFact Card fields
